<title>USA: U.S. House refuses to alter sugar loan program.</title>
<headline>U.S. House refuses to alter sugar loan program.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-07-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>The U.S. House rejected on Thursday a proposal to alter the sugar loan program, a step that proponents said would reduce an absurdly high domestic price for sugar.</p>
<p>The amendment was defeated, 175-253. It was a far larger margin than one year ago when an attempt to derail the sugar program failed by less than 10 votes.</p>
</text>
